  23: actor's transcript. (If hooks had not fired, the command was a no-op: "Already on 'main'".)
  24: 
  25: ## Instrument 2 â€” the documentation (claude-code-guide agent)
  26: 
  27: - "Hooks from settings files ... also run inside subagents. When a subagent calls a tool, tool
  28:   events such as `PreToolUse` and `PostToolUse` fire the same configured hooks as in the main
  29:   conversation, and the input carries the `agent_id` and `agent_type` fields" (hooks-guide, "How
  30:   hooks work").
  31: - The spawn tool's name for matchers is **`Agent`** (tools-reference; there is no separate Task
  32:   tool name in current versions).
  33: - PreToolUse deny with a model-visible reason: JSON `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision:
  34:   "deny"` + `permissionDecisionReason` â€” "cancel the tool call and send the reason to Claude".
  35: - PostToolUse: exit code 2 "shows stderr to Claude; the tool already ran" â€” the channel for a
  36:   model-visible per-tool alarm.
  37: - UserPromptSubmit: exit 0 stdout is injected into context (the stamp already relies on this).
  38: - Mid-session settings edits: "the file watcher normally picks up hook changes automatically" â€”
  39:   the docs claim no session-start freeze. Not independently measured; flagged for a post-merge
  40:   check rather than relied on.
  41: 
  42: ## Instrument 3 â€” headless probe with log-everything hooks (decisive)
  43: 
  44: A scratchpad project with `probe-settings.json` (committed beside this file): PreToolUse and
  45: PostToolUse hooks with NO matcher, each appending its full stdin JSON to `pre.jsonl` /
  46: `post.jsonl`. Two headless runs (`claude -p --settings probe-settings.json`):
  47: 
  48: **Run 1** (prompt mangled by native-argument quoting, still informative): the top-level session
  49: ran Bash and spawned one general-purpose subagent; that subagent used Skill, Glob, Read, Grep and
  50: PowerShell. `pre-run1.jsonl` / `post-run1.jsonl` show PreToolUse AND PostToolUse events for every
  51: one of those subagent tool calls, each carrying `agent_id` + `agent_type=general-purpose`, plus a
  52: top-level `tool=Agent` PreToolUse event, plus events from a further nested headless session.
  53: 
  54: **Run 2** (prompt piped via stdin, clean): top level spawns agent A; agent A spawns agent B. The
  55: complete `pre-run2.jsonl`, four lines total across both files:
  56: 
  57: ```
  58: PreToolUse   tool=Agent  agent_id=(empty)            session=c15ee2f2   <- top-level spawn
  59: PreToolUse   tool=Agent  agent_id=a19066bbe5c4b7eb7  agent_type=general-purpose   <- AGENT A'S OWN SPAWN OF AGENT B
  60: PostToolUse  tool=Agent  agent_id=a19066bbe5c4b7eb7  agent_type=general-purpose   <- B completed, seen from inside A
  61: PostToolUse  tool=Agent  agent_id=(empty)            session=c15ee2f2   <- A completed, top level
  62: ```
  63: 
  64: The second line is the deployment case verbatim: an Agent call made INSIDE a spawned agent (the
  65: conductor-spawns-a-sitting shape) passes through PreToolUse, and the payload identifies the
  66: spawning subagent. Raw evidence: `hookprobe/*.jsonl`, the probe settings, and the run-2 prompt,
  67: all in this directory.
  68: 
  69: ## Consequences for the build
  70: 
  71: 1. The PreToolUse gate matched to `Agent` guards EVERY spawn boundary in the relay â€” coordinator
  72:    â†’ conductor, conductor â†’ sitting, conductor â†’ reviewer-runner, orchestrator â†’ executor and
  73:    mechanical â€” from one hook entry. No per-contract fallback text is needed.
  74: 2. Deny shape: JSON `permissionDecision: "deny"` with the reason string; the reason reaches the
  75:    denied actor, so the parking choreography rides IN the deny reason.
  76: 3. Alarm shape: PostToolUse, exit 2 + stderr, fires inside subagents too â€” every actor hears it.
  77: 4. The stamp alarm rides UserPromptSubmit stdout as the stamp already does. UserPromptSubmit does
  78:    not fire inside subagents (docs are silent on it; no such event appeared in any probe log) â€”
  79:    which is why the item's design carries the PostToolUse alarm for agents and the stamp alarm
  80:    for the founder-facing session, and both are needed.
  81: 5. One caution kept from run 1: PowerShell native-argument quoting mangled a nested prompt. The
  82:    drill therefore feeds hook stdin via files/pipes, never as inline quoted JSON arguments.

